@HostAddress = http://localhost:5110

# Every POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE must send X-Requested-With: Lorebound (CSRF check).

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

###

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "player@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery", "displayName": "Player" }

###

# Sets the lorebound.auth cookie (Secure: use the https profile in a browser).
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "player@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery", "rememberMe": false }

###

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

###

# userId and code come from the [dev email] link in the API log.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/confirm-email
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "<userId>", "code": "<code>" }

###

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/resend-confirmation
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "player@example.com" }

###

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/forgot-password
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "player@example.com" }

###

# email and code come from the [dev email] reset link in the API log.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/reset-password
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "player@example.com", "code": "<code>", "newPassword": "a brand new passphrase" }

###

### Update setting

PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Osepia Revised",
  "description": "Updated setting description."
}

### Delete setting

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

# Needs the cookie from a login above.
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/users/me

###

PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/users/me
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Renamed Player" }

###

### Create an invite (GameMaster). Body is optional.

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/invites
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expiresInDays": 7, "maxUses": 5 }

###

### List invites (GameMaster)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/invites

### Revoke an invite (GameMaster)

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/invites/<INVITE_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

###

### Preview an invite (any signed-in user). Case and hyphens are ignored.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/invites/<CODE>

###

### Create setting

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/settings
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Osepia",
  "description": "A campaign setting inspired by the ancient Near East."
}

###

### List settings

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings?search=Osepia&role=gm&page=1&pageSize=20

###

### Get setting detail

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>

###

### Accept an invite (any signed-in user). Safe to repeat.

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/invites/<CODE>/accept
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

###

### List members (any member)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/members

### Change a member's role (owner only)

PATCH {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/members/<USER_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "GameMaster" }

###

### Remove a member, or leave (your own user id)

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/members/<USER_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

###

### List entries (any member). Players never see GM-only entries.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/entries?type=Location&search=tower&page=1&pageSize=20

###

### Create an entry (GameMaster)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/entries
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sharn",
  "entryType": "Location",
  "description": "The City of Towers.",
  "isGmOnly": false
}

###

### Get an entry with its relationships (any member; GM-only entries are 404 for Players)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/entries/<ENTRY_ID>

###

### Update an entry (GameMaster). Replaces every field.

PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/entries/<ENTRY_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sharn",
  "entryType": "Location",
  "description": "The City of Towers, capital of crime.",
  "isGmOnly": true
}

###

### Delete an entry (GameMaster). 409 with relationshipCount and characterCount if it has relationships or characters chose it; ?force=true deletes its relationships too and leaves those characters with a null choice.

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/entries/<ENTRY_ID>?force=false
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

###

### List relationships (any member). entryId matches either end; Players never see links to GM-only entries.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/relationships?entryId=<ENTRY_ID>&type=Capital%20of&page=1&pageSize=20

###

### Link two entries (GameMaster). Both must belong to this setting; 409 if the same link exists.

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/relationships
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceEntryId": "<ENTRY_ID>",
  "targetEntryId": "<OTHER_ENTRY_ID>",
  "relationshipType": "Capital of",
  "description": "Since the Last War."
}

###

### Change a relationship's type and description (GameMaster). Source and target cannot change.

PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/relationships/<RELATIONSHIP_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "relationshipType": "Largest city of",
  "description": "And the richest."
}

###

### Delete a relationship (GameMaster). The entries stay.

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/relationships/<RELATIONSHIP_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

###

### Suggested relationship types (any signed-in user). Other text is accepted too.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/relationship-types

###

### The builder step catalog (P7-01): 8 ordered steps, the same for every character.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/builder/steps

###

### Options for one builder step (owner with write access), narrowed by earlier choices when any option is linked to them.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/characters/<CHARACTER_ID>/steps/culture/options

###

### Save one step's answer (owner with write access): entryIds for entry steps, freeText for motivation; neither clears it.

PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/characters/<CHARACTER_ID>/choices/culture
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entryIds": ["<ENTRY_ID>"]
}

###

PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/characters/<CHARACTER_ID>/choices/motivation
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "freeText": "Find the mentor who vanished in the Mourning."
}

###

### Start a draft character in a setting you belong to (any member). Name is optional.

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/characters
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "settingId": "<SETTING_ID>",
  "name": "Aster"
}

###

### One character with its choices (its owner, or a GameMaster of its setting).

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/characters/<CHARACTER_ID>

###

### Your own characters, most recently updated first. Optional: status (Draft/Complete), settingId, search, page, pageSize.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/characters?status=Draft&search=aster

###

### Rename a character and set its free-text backstory (owner, while still a member of the setting).

PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/characters/<CHARACTER_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aster Vane",
  "backstory": "Born in the shadow of the towers."
}

###

### Delete your character and its choices (owner only, also after leaving the setting).

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/characters/<CHARACTER_ID>
X-Requested-With: Lorebound

###

### Every character in a setting, removed players' included (GameMaster). Optional: status, search, page, pageSize.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/settings/<SETTING_ID>/characters?status=Complete

###

### Delete your account (needs your password). 409 lists owned settings that still have other members.

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/users/me
X-Requested-With: Lorebound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "<YOUR_PASSWORD>"
}

###
